{# ============================================================
		BASE LAYOUT  —  src/_includes/base.njk
	 ============================================================

	 This is the master layout that wraps every page on the site.
	 Think of it as the skeleton HTML that every page shares.

	 HOW LAYOUTS WORK IN ELEVENTY:
	 ----------------------------
	 Each page file (like index.njk) specifies `layout: base.njk`
	 in its front matter.  Eleventy then:
		 1. Renders the page content
		 2. Injects it into {{ content | safe }} below
		 3. Outputs the complete HTML file

	 The `| safe` filter tells Nunjucks "this content is already
	 HTML, don't escape the < and > characters."

	 FRONT MATTER VARIABLES:
	 ----------------------
	 Pages can set these in their front matter (the --- block):
		 title          → Used in <title> and meta tags (falls back to site.name)
		 description    → Meta description (falls back to site.description)
		 bodyClass      → CSS classes on <body> (default: "d-flex h-100")
		 mainClass      → CSS classes on <main> (default: none)
		 containerClass → Bootstrap container variant wrapping <main> + footer
		                  (default: "container"). Use "container-fluid" for a
		                  full-width page (e.g. wide data tables), or one of the
		                  responsive variants like "container-xxl".
		 cover          → true = "cover page" layout: <main> is centred
		                  vertically between the navbar and the footer
		                  (Bootstrap's Cover example). Used by the home page;
		                  set it on 404/403-style splash pages too. Without it,
		                  content starts right under the navbar and the footer
		                  still sticks to the bottom on short pages.
		 gallery        → true = load PhotoSwipe (see `loadPhotoswipe` below)

		 SEO / sharing knobs (robots, locale, ogImage + ogImageAlt/-Width/
		 -Height/-Type, ogType: article + date:, schemaType, lastmod (quoted),
		 jsonLd, breadcrumbSchema) are listed at the top of head-meta.njk.
		 `llms: false` leaves a page out of /llms.txt (src/llms.njk).

	 PER-PAGE EXTRAS (head + scripts):
	 ---------------------------------
	 Pages inject extra <head> stylesheets and end-of-body scripts via
	 frontmatter arrays — NOT via Nunjucks `{% block %}`.

	 Why: with `layout: base.njk` frontmatter, Eleventy renders the page
	 standalone before injecting it into `{{ content | safe }}`, so child
	 `{% block %}` overrides never reach this parent. Frontmatter-driven
	 arrays are Eleventy's recommended per-page-extras mechanism.

	 Example frontmatter:
		 extraCss: ["/assets/css/expiry.css"]
		 extraScripts:
		   - { src: "https://cdn.sheetjs.com/.../xlsx.full.min.js", cdn: true }
		   - "/assets/js/expiry.js"

	 See the inline comments at the loop sites below for full schema.
	 ============================================================ #}

<!DOCTYPE html>
{# `dd-font-override` turns on the custom font stack in style.css §1.0.
	 Off by default so Bootstrap's / the Bootswatch theme's own font is used.
	 Flip site.fontOverride to true when you set googleFontsUrl.
	 (theme-init only adds/removes its own classes, so this one is safe.) #}
<html lang="{{ site.lang }}" class="h-100{% if site.fontOverride %} dd-font-override{% endif %}">
<head>
	{# --- SEO meta tags (charset, viewport, title, description, Open Graph) ---
		 FIRST in <head> on purpose: head-meta.njk starts with <meta charset>,
		 and the HTML spec wants the charset declaration completely inside
		 the first 1024 bytes of the file. The inline theme-init script used
		 to come first and had pushed it to byte ~789. head-meta has no CSS,
		 so moving it up doesn't affect the anti-flash ordering below.
		 Keep <meta charset> as the first tag in head-meta.njk. #}
	{% include "head-meta.njk" %}

	{# --- Theme init (must run before any CSS to prevent FOUC) --- #}
	{% include "theme-init.njk" %}

	{# --- Does this page need PhotoSwipe (the image lightbox)? ---
		 Yes when the page content contains a lightbox item (the required
		 "dd-pswp" class, see dd-lightbox.js) or the page sets
		 `gallery: true` in its front matter (use that when the gallery
		 sits in a layout or include rather than in the page itself).
		 Every other page skips PhotoSwipe's two scripts at the end of
		 <body> (~69 KB minified, ~21 KB over the wire). A page that only
		 MENTIONS the class in its text loads them needlessly — harmless.

		 `content` here is the page's already-rendered HTML (a string),
		 and Nunjucks' `in` operator does a substring test on strings.
		 Variables set here are visible inside the includes below, so
		 head-assets.njk tests `loadPhotoswipe` for PhotoSwipe's
		 stylesheet as well. #}
	{% set loadPhotoswipe = gallery or ("dd-pswp" in content) %}

	{# --- CSS, fonts, favicons, analytics --- #}
	{% include "head-assets.njk" %}

	{# --- Bootswatch switcher: saved theme in place BEFORE first paint ---
		 (dev tool: only while site.bootswatchSwitcher is true)

		 1. window.ddBootswatchSheets = { name: [url, sri], … } for every
		    theme in src/_data/cdn.js plus "default" (plain Bootstrap).
		    bootswatch-switcher.js uses the same map for clicks, so the
		    URLs and hashes are written in ONE place (cdn.js).
		 2. head-assets.njk has just written the site's default theme
		    <link>. If the visitor picked another theme, swap that link's
		    href here, while the parser is still in <head>: nothing has
		    been painted yet, and a stylesheet the PARSER created stays
		    render-blocking, so the first paint already uses the saved
		    theme. (This used to happen at DOMContentLoaded, after a
		    first paint in the default theme: a flash on every page.)
		    blocking="render" says the same thing explicitly.
		 3. SRI still applies (integrity from the map; crossorigin is
		    already on the tag). If the file fails, onerror puts the
		    default back.
		 Costs ~5.5 KB of HTML per page while the switcher is on (most
		 of it the 27 hashes) — one more reason to switch it off on a
		 finished site. #}
	{% if site.bootswatchSwitcher %}
	<script>
	(function () {
		var sheets = window.ddBootswatchSheets = {
			"default": [{{ cdn.bootstrap.css.url | dump | safe }}, {{ cdn.bootstrap.css.integrity | dump | safe }}]{% for name, sheet in cdn.bootswatch.themes %},
			{{ name | dump | safe }}: [{{ sheet.url | dump | safe }}, {{ sheet.integrity | dump | safe }}]{% endfor %}
		};
		var link = document.getElementById("bootswatch-theme") || document.getElementById("bootstrap-default");
		var saved = window.ddStore ? ddStore.get("bootswatchTheme") : null;
		if (!link || !saved || !Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(sheets, saved)) return;
		var current = link.id === "bootstrap-default" ? "default" : {{ (site.defaultBootswatchTheme or "default") | dump | safe }};
		if (saved === current) return;

		var original = { id: link.id, href: link.href, integrity: link.integrity };
		link.onerror = function () {
			link.onerror = null;
			link.id = original.id;
			link.integrity = original.integrity;
			link.href = original.href;
			if (window.ddTheme) ddTheme.setBootswatch(current);
		};
		link.setAttribute("blocking", "render");
		link.id = saved === "default" ? "bootstrap-default" : "bootswatch-theme";
		link.integrity = sheets[saved][1];
		link.href = sheets[saved][0];
	})();
	</script>
	{% endif %}

	{# --- Page-specific stylesheets ---
		 Pages opt in via the `extraCss:` frontmatter array. Each entry is
		 an href string. Local paths get the build's cache-bust query
		 appended automatically; anything starting with `http` is passed
		 through untouched so external CDN stylesheets keep their own
		 versioning intact.

		 Why frontmatter and not `{% block head %}`? Eleventy's `layout:`
		 frontmatter renders the page standalone first, then injects the
		 rendered HTML into `{{ content | safe }}` here — so child-template
		 `{% block %}` overrides don't reach the parent. Frontmatter is the
		 official Eleventy-way of passing per-page extras to a layout.

		 Load order: these come AFTER high-contrast.css (head-assets.njk),
		 so a page rule with equal specificity beats an HC rule that isn't
		 !important. Write page CSS with Bootstrap tokens (var(--bs-*)) so
		 the HC token map still recolours it. #}
	{% if extraCss %}{% for href in extraCss %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ href }}{% if href.indexOf("http") != 0 %}?v={{ cacheBust }}{% endif %}">
	{% endfor %}{% endif %}
</head>

{# `cover-container` is only a hook (named after Bootstrap's Cover example)
	 for cover pages — style.css has no rule for it; add one there if a cover
	 page ever needs page-level styling. #}
<body class="{{ bodyClass | default('d-flex h-100') }}{% if cover %} cover-container{% endif %}">

	{# --- Skip-to-content (accessibility — visible on focus) ---
		 .visually-hidden-focusable keeps it off-screen until it gets keyboard
		 focus. position-fixed + .dd-skip-link (z-index in style.css §2.1)
		 put it ABOVE the fixed navbar — before, it was painted underneath
		 the blue bar and the first Tab stop looked like nothing happened.
		 btn-light (not btn-primary) so it stands out against bg-primary. #}
	<a class="dd-skip-link visually-hidden-focusable position-fixed top-0 start-0 m-2 btn btn-light btn-sm shadow" href="#content">Skip to main content</a>

	{# --- Fixed-top navbar --- #}
	{% include "navbar.njk" %}

	{# --- Offcanvas navigation menu --- #}
	{% include "offcanvas-menu.njk" %}

	{# --- Page content wrapper --- #}
	<div id="dd-page" class="w-100 d-flex flex-column">
		<div class="{{ containerClass | default('container') }} d-flex w-100 h-100 p-3 mx-auto flex-column">

			{# --- Flex spacer (cover pages only) — its mb-auto and the
				 footer's mt-auto split the free height, so <main> ends up
				 vertically centred. Without the spacer, only the footer's
				 mt-auto is left: content sits at the top, footer at the
				 bottom (a classic "sticky footer"). --- #}
			{% if cover %}<div class="mb-auto"></div>{% endif %}

			<main id="content"{% if mainClass %} class="{{ mainClass }}"{% endif %}>
				{# --- Page content gets injected here --- #}
				{{ content | safe }}
			</main>

			{% include "footer.njk" %}

		</div>
	</div>

	{# --- Third-party scripts (jsDelivr) ---
		 URLs and SRI hashes come from src/_data/cdn.js, the one place to
		 bump a version. crossorigin="anonymous" is required for SRI on a
		 cross-origin file.
		 PhotoSwipe only on pages that need it (`loadPhotoswipe`, set in
		 <head> above); dd-lightbox.js checks for both globals, so a page
		 without them is fine. #}
	<script src="{{ cdn.bootstrap.js.url }}"
					integrity="{{ cdn.bootstrap.js.integrity }}"
					crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
	{% if loadPhotoswipe %}
	<script src="{{ cdn.photoswipe.js.url }}"
					integrity="{{ cdn.photoswipe.js.integrity }}"
					crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
	<script src="{{ cdn.photoswipe.lightboxJs.url }}"
					integrity="{{ cdn.photoswipe.lightboxJs.integrity }}"
					crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
	{% endif %}
	{# --- Site-wide JS bundle ---
		 One request instead of one per file. The bundle is concatenated
		 at build time by the "JS BUNDLING" section in eleventy.config.js
		 from separate source files in src/assets/js/. Which files, in
		 which order, and which only on a site.json condition: the
		 SITE_WIDE_JS list at the top of eleventy.config.js (e.g.
		 bootswatch-switcher only when site.bootswatchSwitcher is true).
		 Edit the source files as usual — every build (and every --watch
		 rebuild) regenerates the bundle. #}
	<script src="/assets/js/bundle.js?v={{ cacheBust }}"></script>

	{# --- Page-specific scripts ---
		 Pages opt in via the `extraScripts:` frontmatter array. Each entry
		 is either a string (interpreted as a local non-module script — gets
		 cache-bust appended) or an object with shape:
			 { src, type?, cdn?, integrity?, crossorigin? }
		 - `type: "module"` emits a module script (for ES-module entry points).
		 - `cdn: true` skips the cache-bust suffix (use for third-party CDN URLs).
		 - `integrity` + `crossorigin` pass through to the <script> tag (SRI).
		 See the `extraCss` comment in <head> for why this is frontmatter-driven
		 rather than `{% block scripts %}`. #}
	{% if extraScripts %}{% for s in extraScripts %}{% if s is string %}<script src="{{ s }}?v={{ cacheBust }}"></script>
	{% else %}<script {% if s.type %}type="{{ s.type }}" {% endif %}src="{{ s.src }}{% if not s.cdn %}?v={{ cacheBust }}{% endif %}"{% if s.integrity %} integrity="{{ s.integrity }}"{% endif %}{% if s.crossorigin %} crossorigin="{{ s.crossorigin }}"{% endif %}></script>
	{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}

	{# --- Cookie / storage notice — informational, non-blocking ---
		 dfault.js shows #dd-cookie-toast once and remembers the dismissal
		 in localStorage. Keep the id: the JS hooks onto it.

		 - .toast-container is Bootstrap's own wrapper (z-index token 1090),
		   replacing the old hand-rolled style="z-index:1055".
		 - The live region (role="status" aria-live="polite") sits on that
		   always-present wrapper, not on the toast. The toast starts as
		   display:none, and screen readers only announce content that
		   appears inside a live region which already existed. (role="alert"
		   + aria-live="polite" was a contradiction: alert is assertive.)
		 - Plain .btn-close: in Bootstrap 5.3 it turns white by itself under
		   data-bs-theme="dark" (set on <html> by theme-init). The old
		   .btn-close-white is deprecated and drew a white X on the light
		   toast, so light-mode visitors couldn't see the only dismiss button.
		 - The copy says what the site really does: no cookies of its own,
		   preferences in localStorage, files from public CDNs; GA only when
		   site.gaId is set. Keep it in sync with legal.njk.
		 - CONSENT MODE (site.json → gaConsent "required", with a gaId):
		   the toast ASKS instead of informing. Accept / Decline sit inside
		   .toast-body, look the same (refusing must be as easy as
		   accepting — no bright "Accept" next to a grey "Decline"), and
		   replace the X, so closing can't be mistaken for an answer.
		   data-dd-consent="required" tells dfault.js which mode it is;
		   data-dd-consent-choice is what the button stores. Both buttons
		   also carry data-bs-dismiss="toast", so Bootstrap hides the toast. #}
	{% set consentRequired = site.gaId and site.gaConsent == "required" %}
	<div class="toast-container position-fixed bottom-0 start-50 translate-middle-x p-3" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
		<div id="dd-cookie-toast" class="toast align-items-center text-center shadow-sm" data-bs-autohide="false"{% if consentRequired %} data-dd-consent="required"{% endif %}>
			<div class="d-flex">
				<div class="toast-body small">
					<i class="bi bi-cookie me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
					{% if consentRequired %}May we use Google Analytics cookies to count visits? Nothing is sent to Google unless you accept.{% elif site.gaId %}This site uses Google Analytics cookies to count visits.{% else %}No tracking cookies here.{% endif %}
					Your theme choice is saved in your browser, and styles and scripts load from public CDNs.
					<a href="/legal/#cookie-policy">Details</a>
					{% if consentRequired %}
					<div class="d-flex justify-content-center gap-2 mt-2">
						<button type="button" class="btn btn-sm dd-btn-ghost" data-dd-consent-choice="granted" data-bs-dismiss="toast">Accept</button>
						<button type="button" class="btn btn-sm dd-btn-ghost" data-dd-consent-choice="denied" data-bs-dismiss="toast">Decline</button>
					</div>
					{% endif %}
				</div>
				{% if not consentRequired %}
				<button type="button" class="btn-close me-2 m-auto" data-bs-dismiss="toast" aria-label="Close"></button>
				{% endif %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	{# --- HC SVG duotone filter (referenced by high-contrast.css for .high-contrast-custom) --- #}
	{% include "hc-svg-filters.njk" %}

</body>
</html>
